  "row_count": 20,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol. \n1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ . \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 9.209 + 0.338 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.911 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=9.209\\times10^{H3}T+0.169\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.911\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-3.066$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 28.900 - 0.051 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 1.163 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 78.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 28.900 + 0.051 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 1.163 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 39.275 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 22.113 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 25.397 - 2.463 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 0.009 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 56.950 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 25.397 + 2.463 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} - 0.009 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 28.475 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 33.582 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K based on Prusaczyk (101). Other data based on Prusaczyk (101) and Shimauchi (107). ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Phase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol.",
      "1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ .",
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
      "298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 9.209 + 0.338 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.911 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$",
      "$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=9.209\\times10^{H3}T+0.169\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.911\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-3.066$",
      "Reaction equations (kcal/mol):",
      "298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 28.900 - 0.051 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 1.163 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 78.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 28.900 + 0.051 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 1.163 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 39.275 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 22.113 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 25.397 - 2.463 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 0.009 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 56.950 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 25.397 + 2.463 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} - 0.009 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 28.475 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 33.582 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "Sources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K based on Prusaczyk (101). Other data based on Prusaczyk (101) and Shimauchi (107)."
    ],
